// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" - confirmed BOOT button. This
// board's pins_arduino.h has no BOOT alias, but independent ESPHome
// hardware configs for this exact product (devices.esphome.io/devices/
// waveshare-6ch-relay and raw.githubusercontent.com/ryansch/esphome-
// config/main/waveshare-esp32-s3-relay-6ch.yaml) both define a "Boot
// Button" binary_sensor on GPIO0 (inverted/pulled-up, standard
// active-low BOOT-strap button), consistent with this chip's own
// pinNotes "0": "Must be HIGH for normal boot". Corroborated by the
// spotpear.com product-guide mirror ("GP0 - BOOT button - BOOT button
// control pin").
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO38 tagged "led_neopixel" - confirmed onboard WS2812
// RGB status LED. This board's own pins_arduino.h declares
// `#define PIN_RGB_LED 38`. Independently corroborated by the same
// ESPHome configs (light platform esp32_rmt_led_strip, chipset ws2812,
// pin: GPIO38) and by spotpear.com ("WS2812 RGB colorful LED -
// Controllable via GPIO38 pin"). The six relay-drive GPIOs (1, 2, 41,
// 42, 45, 46 per CNX Software's teardown) are separate transistor-
// driven relay outputs, not LEDs, and are left untouched.
